# Story 34: Four Input Modes (50s)
# Hook: One pane, four modes. Double-Escape cycles through them all.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-034-four-input-modes.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
One pane, four modes. Double-Escape cycles through them all.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Start rysh and you land in shell mode -- the greater-than prompt runs commands in your PTY.

[00:08.0 --> 00:18.0]
Double-press Escape. The prompt becomes a less-than sign -- that's prompt mode, where input goes to your AI agent with its own output stream.

[00:18.0 --> 00:28.0]
Double-Escape again and the prompt turns to hash-hash. This is rysh mode for built-in system commands.

[00:28.0 --> 00:38.0]
Once more and the prompt shows an at-sign -- chat mode, a separate AI chat with its own buffer.

[00:38.0 --> 00:46.0]
A final double-Escape brings you full circle back to shell. Greater-than, less-than, hash-hash, at-sign.

[00:46.0 --> 00:50.0]
Four markers, one key. Each mode keeps its own stream.

